{i===22&&<AdSlot id="article-04-later-verses" kind="article"/>}
</>)}
</div>
<section class="closing"><h2>Why the advice still matters</h2><p>Many readers remember these lines because they can be repeated within a family. But a careful reading does more than collect memorable sayings. It asks why Fierro values solidarity after separation, praises work after losing his livelihood, and warns against violence when violence has shaped his own story.</p><p>The most celebrated call for unity is therefore both a moral aspiration and an answer to painful experience. The poem invites reflection, not an uncritical portrait of its narrator as a perfect father.</p><h2>Sources and reading companions</h2><ul><li><a href="/leer/vuelta/32/" lang="es">Canto XXXII · original Spanish text, in our structured reader</a></li><li><a href="/consejos-martin-fierro/" lang="es">Spanish edition with vocabulary annotations</a></li><li><a href="/en/characters/">The characters of Martín Fierro</a></li><li><a href="/en/library/themes-and-analysis/">Themes, symbols and literary analysis</a></li><li><a href="/en/martin-fierro-summary/">English plot summary: both parts</a></li></ul><p><strong>Text integrity:</strong> the original lines above are read dynamically from the existing repository corpus. No verse text has been rewritten, normalized or independently reconstructed for this page.</p></section>
